# fixedbugs, defect 2061, lane b17-ffi, 2026-10-14.
#
# The control beside the defect: `absval` names `myabs`, a macro written with
# parameters, and the header declares a function `myabs` beside it, so the
# probe's `(absval)(a0)` reaches a declaration and the build is not refused;
# the call expands both macros, `1000.0`, as C reads the header. The walk the
# repair added is asked only on a refused build, and this one builds.

extern "fixedbugs-2061-beside.h"
    function absval(x: f64) -> f64

function main()
    print(absval(-3.0))
